    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1049">

                <pb facs="0790" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1093</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-24T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 24, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. If annulment or modification of mining decree has not yet been accomplished in
                    accordance with Department’s March 13, 6 p.m., you will, in view present unusual
                    circumstances, and impossibility for many interested Americans to pay their
                    taxes before April 1, immediately concentrate your best efforts to secure, as a
                    temporary expedient, longest possible extension in time for payment of this
                    tercio’s tax, in order that more time may be available for negotiations.</p>
                <p>Telegraph status and prospects.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
